 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were broken,\nSat cowering near their partner's shoulder;\nAnd there in agitation and anxiety,\nThe disconsolate guests began cry.\nJOHN on his knees before the table,\nWith snatched cup of water, all forsook him,\nAnd, passing over to an device,\nReferred a postilion who testified\nHe had not much taste for this boorish horse,\nBut he was from himself like a rabbit;\nSo came upon his country doctor,\nWho at first survey'd his situation but",
